1966+ D360              ; BumpTriggerTable - sprites que disparan acción al "chocar" (no por overlap).
1967+ D360              ; ==============================================================================
1968+ D360              ; Cada entry: ptr (DEFW), required_key (DEFB), action_id (DEFB). 4 bytes.
1969+ D360              ; Terminada en DEFW 0.
1970+ D360              ;
1971+ D360              ; Action_ids:
1972+ D360              ;   1 = TownHall: ChurchKeySpawned = 1, CurrentKey = 0.
1973+ D360              ;   2 = ChurchDoor: ChurchDoorOpen = 1, CurrentKey = 0, reescribe ptr de la
1974+ D360              ;       entry a BgGfx_old_church_door_open + rebuild CollisionMap.
1975+ D360              ;
1976+ D360              ; El sprite tiene que estar también en WallAlwaysTable para que sea sólido.
1977+ D360              ;
1978+ D360              ; NOTA: el cutscene final (action 3 = TownGate) se dispara aparte, en
1979+ D360              ; CheckTownGateTriggerBg (town_gate_cutscene.asm). El arco es BG sprite y
1980+ D360              ; no esta en PickupTable, asi que esta tabla no puede hospedarlo. La logica
1981+ D360              ; es equivalente: AABB del player vs rect del arco con tolerancia +-4.
1982+ D360              ; ==============================================================================
1983+ D360              BumpTriggerTable:
1984+ D360 01 E2            DEFW BgGfx_old_church_door_closed
1985+ D362 05               DEFB 5                          ; key requerida = ChurchKey
